webmvs patch 0019: checkpoint staging.

The checkpoint command (patches 0015, 0018) writes the shadow-file copies (full checkpoint) or shadows.dlt
(delta) and machine.srf straight into the slot directory on OPFS while the CPUs are stopped. In the browser
every OPFS file create, write, fsync and close is a round trip to the WasmFS OPFS proxy thread (Firefox:
30-50 ms per file, Chromium 3-5 ms), so most of the pause was file I/O. With stage=<dir> (browser default
/tmp/ckpt-stage, the WasmFS memory backend) these files are written into memory during the pause and copied
into the slot after sr_start_cpus(); the crc32 of machine.srf is taken from the staged copy (same bytes);
checkpoint.json is still written last, so the slot becomes valid only when everything is there.
New: option stage=<dir> (stage= turns it off; native default off), "storeMs" in checkpoint.json, and
", store %d ms" at the end of the HHC02030I text (after the 0018 suffix). Needs 0015, 0017 and 0018.
The staged machine.srf and shadows.dlt get their capacity once before the pause (largest size so far
+ 25 %): a WasmFS memory file keeps its capacity when it is opened again with O_TRUNC, so the small writes
do not grow and copy the buffer at every checkpoint.

